{"c":[{"name":"20261023T144151Z-19beeb928bb79a4a","text":"Measured 2026-10-23: a bare full pytest run in a torch-provisioned checkout drops torch midway: test_coverage_collection runs make coverage-engine, whose sync is exact. Later torch-gated tests fail (No module named torch.distributed); ensure-env, then rerun them.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261023T152930Z-94e11b6c634d81a7","text":"DuckDB 2.0.0, measured 2026-10-23: a zstd-column file opened read-only with a .wal (killed ingest) lists the replayed rows in pragma_storage_info as persistent=false, Uncompressed; every persistent segment is ZSTD. A zstd check must filter persistent or run with no .wal.","type":"note"}]}
